{"kind":"assert","text":"Supplemental correction to report870 (9665a035ead4ea3434e75487876da9aabad7d454), at the requester's direction. This supplements that report without retiring it. CLOSE-01–04, the gate/threat mapping and the bounded P1e scope remain unchanged. No source changes, builds, adoption or activation were performed.\n\nMy section4C ordering D \u003c R \u003c root ratification(D) was incorrect for GitSeq's ordinary decision-adoption path. The current primary /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq/SKILL.md:484–491 says: “On the ordinary path, propose and ratify before requesting review,” and requires the review request to rest on the ratified proposal and artifact. docs/reference/gs/ratify.md reserves report ratification to the live review requester. internal/reviewguard/binding.go:399–450 requires a standing ratified proposal for the self-initiated binding. These primary files were checked at clean source d630554a7ba7d99c5f95eb77e1dfa7fd1f41637a.\n\nReplace section4C's ordering with this exact ordinary-path contract:\nsource S and its decision artifact A, plus actual evidence E -\u003e proposal D resting on A and binding the exact S/profile/E/case/decision manifest -\u003e root ratification AD of D -\u003e review request Q resting on D, AD and every exact artifact to be reviewed -\u003e independent review promise P -\u003e guarded review R at S -\u003e the review requester's ratification AR of R. Require D \u003c AD \u003c Q \u003c P \u003c R \u003c AR \u003c= the verified frontier F, with the full same-genesis causal bindings, not just timestamps. AD and AR each rest on exactly their one target under GitSeq's ratify rule. D's proposal text should plainly adopt the decision recorded by A at S, with its exact detached E and manifest binding; it is not an unattached new kind of adoption token.\n\nD must explicitly state the conditional effect: root selects D1–D9 for the named source/profile, but no Noseq gate activation is authorized by D or AD alone. The independent approved R, AR, all exact evidence/authority checks and the separately commissioned operational scope must also hold. GitSeq correctly records D as ratified immediately; the application of that conditional decision remains blocked while its predicates are absent. We are not inventing a “pending ratify” status or treating ratification as unsigned intent.\n\nR's strict signed review text should bind both D and the already-existing AD, along with S, the profile and E digests, exhaustive decisions/cases and the reviewed artifact set. The reviewer is distinct from implementation/manifest author and root. Q/R must use the actual assigned, self-initiated or evidence-only binding appropriate to their artifacts; do not relabel an assigned lifecycle. At F, the verified local fold must identify those exact surviving effective AD and AR, the still-effective D/R, appropriate authority and no disqualifying retirement, superseded source world or unresolved conflicting adoption. An AD retirement/replacement cannot silently reuse R that approved the earlier adoption binding; request fresh review on the current ratified decision.\n\nThe manifest/identity graph remains acyclic. S contains no future E/D/AD/R/AR identifiers; E names S and the fixed profile; D names A/S/E but contains no future review ID; AD names D; Q/P/R name only existing predecessors; AR names R. F is supplied by the external verification context. No signed object contains its own future hash.\n\nNo second adoption proposal or duplicate root ratification after R is needed. Root already adopted the conditional decision through AD. The minimal authority validator can return “all decision predicates verified at F” only after AR and all source/evidence checks succeed; this remains a diagnostic, not a bearer token or a deployment approval. Actual activation remains outside the upcoming bounded P1e commission. When root later authorizes implementation or invocation of a real gate, use an ordinary root request/operational instruction citing D, AD, R, AR and the exact approved source/evidence/frontier, with the intended action and scope explicit. That is execution authority under the same decision, not a second adoption scheme. A request to implement gate wiring is not evidence that its new source has already been reviewed. Changed source still requires its own exact-head evidence/review and any changed decision binding before activation. No final extra signature is cryptographically necessary if the existing conditional decision and a later express commission already authorize that exact operation; do not manufacture another adoption ceremony.\n\nExtend section4I tests to accept the correct D/AD/Q/P/R/AR order and reject review requested before AD, a review that omits/substitutes D or AD, use of an earlier retired AD with a later unrelated ratification, and activation from AD or R alone. Preserve effective-actor, exact-artifact/evidence, active-ratification, offline-frontier and all other negatives from report870. Changes-requested requires corrected exact artifacts and, if the decision itself changes, a new proposal/ratification before fresh review.\n\nA separate dependency-provenance correction also applies to sections4A/D. I independently confirmed the existing /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq/bin/gs has SHA256 0b8aeeec3b31a3aefbd0714e7a1d96286f1cd94bf7746748c5f9e6ae7dc978b6; go version -m reports Go1.27.0, vcs.revision183211c3b5bff170171c5bfbe9bfbc3aacde08f6 and vcs.modified=true. It must not be attributed to the inspected clean d630 source. Under root's forthcoming explicit dev-only build commission, P1e should build a distinct verifier from a clean isolated clone at d630, record exact source/tree, Go toolchain, module/go.sum verification, platform/environment/build flags, build log and binary digest, and exercise its real generated signed chains plus the actual public Noseq export. Leave the current bin/gs, resident, shared native build and live-key custody untouched. No real actor private keys or live configuration are imported. If the pinned fresh verifier cannot validate the current public export, report that concrete incompatibility; do not fall back silently to the unrelated installed binary.\n\nThe existing P1d source/crypto approval is unchanged. Full G1–G5 gates remain closed.","body":{"correction_of":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:9665a035ead4ea3434e75487876da9aabad7d454","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"supplemental advice: ordinary adoption ordering and verifier build provenance; no adoption or activation"}}